{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3d81b6c2-91a4-4f0e-8b57-2c7d4e9a1f36",
    "name": "FlipStar - TIMWE Datasync",
    "description": "The SyncOrderRelation callback TIMWE's Master Aggregator calls when a subscription relationship is created or removed.\n\n## One endpoint, not several\n\nUnlike the OneVAS webhooks, TIMWE carries the operation in the payload rather than the URL. Subscribe, unsubscribe and update all arrive at the same address and differ only in `updateType` (1, 2, 3).\n\n## Reachability\n\n`baseUrl` defaults to the tunnel address `https://172.16.170.2:443`, which resolves **only** from the staging server or from TIMWE's side of the IPsec tunnel. From anywhere else it times out, which is correct rather than a fault.\n\nTo run this from a laptop, either point `baseUrl` at `https://api.uat.flipstar.et` (same code, public path) or open an SSH forward:\n\n```\nssh -L 8443:172.16.170.2:443 root@sky-staging-server\n```\n\nand set `baseUrl` to `https://localhost:8443`.\n\n## Turn off certificate verification\n\nSettings -> General -> **SSL certificate verification: OFF**. The certificate is issued for a hostname, so connecting by IP is a mismatch and every request otherwise fails at the TLS handshake.\n\n## Expect 2032 until products are mapped\n\nThe lookup is `SubscriptionTier.product_id`. Until TIMWE supplies real product IDs and they are set on the tiers, every well-formed request answers 2032. That is documented behaviour, not a bug.\n\n## No authentication\n\nSyncOrderRelation carries no credentials -- the guide states the message header is empty. Access is controlled by source IP (`TIMWE_ALLOWED_IPS`) and by the tunnel itself. An Authorization header is ignored.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Subscription lifecycle",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Subscribe (updateType 1)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "text/xml; charset=utf-8"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "<soapenv:Envelope xmlns:soapenv=\"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/\">\n  <soapenv:Body>\n    <ns1:syncOrderRelation xmlns:ns1=\"http://www.csapi.org/schema/parlayx/data/sync/v1_0/local\">\n      <ns1:userID>\n        <ID>{{msisdn}}</ID>\n        <type>0</type>\n      </ns1:userID>\n      <ns1:spID>{{spID}}</ns1:spID>\n      <ns1:productID>{{productID}}</ns1:productID>\n      <ns1:serviceID>{{serviceID}}</ns1:serviceID>\n      <ns1:serviceList>{{serviceID}}</ns1:serviceList>\n      <ns1:updateType>1</ns1:updateType>\n      <ns1:updateTime>20260901120000</ns1:updateTime>\n      <ns1:updateDesc>Addition</ns1:updateDesc>\n      <ns1:effectiveTime>20260901120000</ns1:effectiveTime>\n      <ns1:expiryTime>20361231160000</ns1:expiryTime>\n      <ns1:extensionInfo>\n        <item><key>transactionID</key><value>{{$guid}}</value></item>\n        <item><key>orderKey</key><value>{{$randomInt}}</value></item>\n        <item><key>keyword</key><value>sub</value></item>\n        <item><key>channelID</key><value>1</value></item>\n      </ns1:extensionInfo>\n    </ns1:syncOrderRelation>\n  </soapenv:Body>\n</soapenv:Envelope>",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "xml"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timwe/sync-order-relation",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "timwe",
                "sync-order-relation"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A user subscribes by SMS or WEB. Creates and activates a SubscriptionPlan once TIMWE_INTEGRATION_ENABLED is on; until then the event is recorded and answered 0."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// The response is SOAP, not JSON. Reading the code by regex rather than",
                  "// xml2Json keeps this independent of how Postman maps namespace prefixes.",
                  "const raw = pm.response.text();",
                  "const codeMatch = raw.match(/<ns1:result>(\\d+)<\\/ns1:result>/);",
                  "const descMatch = raw.match(/<ns1:resultDescription>([^<]*)<\\/ns1:resultDescription>/);",
                  "const code = codeMatch ? codeMatch[1] : null;",
                  "const desc = descMatch ? descMatch[1] : \"\";",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200 with a SOAP body\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"xml\");",
                  "    pm.expect(code, \"no <ns1:result> element in the response\").to.not.be.null;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "console.log(\"result \" + code + \" - \" + desc);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"productID is mapped to a tier\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(",
                  "        code,",
                  "        \"2032 means no SubscriptionTier has product_id=\" +",
                  "            pm.variables.get(\"productID\") +",
                  "            \". Expected until TIMWE supplies the real product IDs.\"",
                  "    ).to.not.eql(\"2032\");",
                  "    pm.expect(code).to.eql(\"0\");",
                  "});",
                  ""
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
